 34NE c  Isotope discovery (2012Th10): Ta({+48}Ca,X) at RIKEN (2002No11) and    
 34NE2c  Ta({+48}Ca,X) at GANIL (2002Lu09).                                     
 34NE c  2002No11: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=64 MeV/nucleon at RIKEN. Projectile fragments
 34NE2c  were separated and identified by the large-acceptance RIKEN            
 34NE3c  Projectile-Fragment Separator (RIPS). Measured production yield and    
 34NE4c  deduced production cross section of {+34}Ne to be |?0.1 pb. Also see   
 34NE5c  annual report 2002NoZY.                                                
 34NE c  2002Lu09: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=59.8 MeV/nucleon at GANIL. Projectile        
 34NE2c  fragments were separated and identified by the LISE-2000 fragment      
 34NE3c  separator. Measured production yield and deduced production cross      
 34NE4c  section of {+34}Ne to be 0.17 pb {I12}. Also see 2002LuZT,2002Lu19,    
 34NE5c  2003Lu11, 2004Lu19.                                                    
 34NE c  2019Ah07: {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X) E=345 MeV/nucleon, 450-pnA {+48}Ca beam at 
 34NE2c  RIKEN. Projectile fragments were separated and identified using        
 34NE3c  |DE-ToF-B|r by the large-acceptance two-stage separator BigRIPS.       
 34NE4c  Optimum settings of B|r were tuned to transmit {+33}F for 14 hours and 
 34NE5c  {+36}Ne+{+39}Na for 7.8 hours. The Be target was irradiated with       
 34NE6c  1.4|*10{+17} and 7.8|*10{+16} {+48}Ca ions, respectively. Measured Z vs
 34NE7c  A/Z particle-identification plot. 115 {+34}Ne events were observed in  
 34NE8c  the {+33}F setting, and 4 {+34}Ne events were observed in the          
 34NE9c  {+36}Ne+{+39}Na setting. No {+35}Ne or {+36}Ne events were observed in 
 34NEAc  either setting.                                                        
 34NE c  2022Ah02: Same experimental setup as 2019Ah07 with 540-pnA {+48}Ca     
 34NE2c  beam. Optimum settings of B|r were tuned to transmit {+39}Na for 46.1  
 34NE3c  hours and {+36}Ne for 25.3 hours. Measured Z vs A/Z                    
 34NE4c  particle-identification plot. Some {+34}Ne events were observed in the 
 34NE5c  {+36}Ne setting. No {+35}Ne or {+36}Ne events were observed in either  
 34NE6c  setting.                                                               
 34NE c  2025Ku15: review of two experiments, 2019Ah07 and 2022Ah02, at RIKEN.  
 34NE2c  No events for {+32}F, {+33}F, {+35}Ne, {+36}Ne, and {+38}Na were       
 34NE3c  observed. The existence of bound {+32}F, {+33}F, {+35}Ne, {+36}Ne, and 
 34NE4c  {+38}Na can be excluded at high confidence level, obtained from        
 34NE5c  zero-event probabilities calculated using expected yields and the      
 34NE6c  Poisson probability distribution. Authors conclude that the most       
 34NE7c  neutron-rich and heaviest bound nuclei of fluorine and neon,           
 34NE8c  corresponding to the dripline nuclei, are {+31}F and {+34}Ne,          
 34NE9c  respectively.                                                          
